        "raw": "<p>Has &#39;Sentinels&#39; taken over your everyday vocabulary ?</p><p>I used say &#39;flip&#39; when I meant &#39;becoming really angry&#39;, as in &quot;Good thing he left, one more minute and I would have flipped.&quot;</p><p>A while ago, I realised &nbsp;that I was starting to use it more in a sense that Villain Cards flip, which in most cases means that they become really unpredictable/crazy/hard to deal with/harder to get rid of. Which, I guess, <em>sounds</em> exactly the same as the other &#39;flip&#39; but , hey, <em>&nbsp;I</em> know that there is a difference.</p><p>(I have had other games which found their way in my everyday vocabulary, for example, I still call all negative effects &#39;Bad Stuff&#39; - a relic from when I still played a lot of Munchkin.)</p><p>So, have you ever encountered your boss on Advance mode? &#39;End of Day&#39;ed an entire project? Referred to someone who was off sick as &#39;Incapped&#39;?</p><p>And more importantly, can you think of any more ways in which Sentinels can &#39;improve&#39; the English language (or at least make it a damn sight more colourful)?</p>",
