        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-07T22:09:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Blossercubbles\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/blossercubbles/48/1863_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Blossercubbles:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I enjoy Mentally Diverging trash around the store. Does that help?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I can't think of anything that's directly on the topic (though I have the feeling I have done something at least once, I just can't recall the specifics), but I do know that playing Sentinels has permanently branded the spelling of several previously-obscure words, such as \"Divergence\", onto my brain.&nbsp; Like Magic the Gathering before it, it has essentially served as a teaching aid in my day-to-day life.</p>",
