      {
        "id": 89758,
        "name": "TheMonocleSpy",
        "username": "TheMonocleSpy",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/7993a0/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-08T02:24:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There's a term our group uses a lot in SOTM and in other games.</p><p>It's based of a card in the Wraith deck called \"Impromptu Invention\" featuring the Wraith holding what looks like a hair dryer rigged as a weapon. Every player in our group dubbed it as being one of the most powerful cards in the game since it allows her to set up her other equipments very quickly. Arguably it is her best card and the first card mentioned to anyone new to playing the Wraith.</p><p>So anytime there's an ability or mechanic that is considered the best for a certain character, we call it their \"hair dryer\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>E.X. Playing D&amp;D with same friends as a conjurer. I keep using teleport, a 5th level spell regarded as my character's \"hair dryer\", since everyone relies on me to transport them places and I'm the only one in the party capable of teleportation.</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
